{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Operator ruling (2026-08-22): the rebar-gerrit-voter-errors alarm fired 5 times in 2 days; investigation proved every incident was a transient, self-healing event handled by designed recovery paths (review timeout -> backfill retry; curl-28 clone stalls under merge-burst load; retryable-gap budgets escalating to the designed fail-closed -1). All affected changes merged with LLM-Review +1; none required operator attention. Ruling: recalibrate the alarm to reduce noise — transient self-healing errors should not page; a SUSTAINED voter failure (the fail-closed gate actually stuck, e.g. expired token, LLM outage, Gerrit down) must still alarm loudly.\n\nCurrent shape (aws describe-alarms, 2026-08-22): metric rebar/host:voter_errors, Sum over period 300s, threshold 0, GreaterThanThreshold, 1 evaluation period, TreatMissingData=notBreaching. I.e. a single marker in any 5-minute window alarms. Terraform source: infra/terraform/monitoring_s4b.tf.\n\nEvidence base for calibration (2-day sample, from journald + CloudWatch):\n- Transient incidents: 1 isolated marker (double-counted to 2 pre-dedup-fix; companion bug fixes that), clearing within one interval. 5 such incidents in 48h under 4-session heavy load.\n- A sustained failure mode emits markers on EVERY review attempt: the webhook queue + backfill reconciler retry continuously, so an expired token / LLM outage produces a continuous marker stream across consecutive intervals, not an isolated spike.\n- Precedents: mirror-guard fix 969acad79b4b (sustained-divergence window, single-sample alarm was incomplete-implementation); operator ruling on 3ff9 (suppress expected-contention noise); CloudWatch replication alarm uses 2x5-min sustained (monitoring_ws7.tf).\n\nDesign constraints:\n- The discriminator is PERSISTENCE, not magnitude: alarm on markers present across consecutive evaluation periods (e.g. N-of-M datapoints > 0, sized so an isolated self-healing error never fires but a stuck gate fires within ~15 minutes), rather than raising the count threshold (a burst of distinct transient errors is still transient; one error repeating forever is the outage).\n- Keep OK/ALARM actions and the fail-closed rationale in the alarm description; update the description to name the calibration rationale and this ticket.\n- Coordinate with the double-count bug fix (companion ticket, blocks this one): calibrate against deduplicated counts.\n- Terraform-only change (monitoring_s4b.tf + any doc). Landing the .tf through Gerrit does NOT apply it: flag in the close comment whether apply happens via the existing drift/apply workflow or needs the operator; do not run terraform apply against AWS yourself without checking how this repo's terraform changes are applied (read infra/ runbooks + terraform-drift.yml first). If apply requires a human, land the change, comment what remains, and close only if the ticket ACs are met by the landed change per repo convention for infra changes (check how prior monitoring_*.tf changes were handled — e.g. the adb6/58a3/mirror-guard lanes).\n\n## Approach\n\nRecalibrate `aws_cloudwatch_metric_alarm.voter_errors` in `infra/terraform/monitoring_s4b.tf`\nfrom single-period (1x300s, Sum>0) to a sustained 3-of-3 consecutive-period shape:\n\n- `period = 300`, `evaluation_periods = 3`, `datapoints_to_alarm = 3`,\n  `threshold = 0`, `comparison_operator = \"GreaterThanThreshold\"`, `statistic = \"Sum\"`,\n  `treat_missing_data = \"notBreaching\"` (all other attributes — namespace/metric,\n  alarm_actions/ok_actions to the shared SNS topic per ticket 9baf, tags — unchanged).\n\nWhy 3-of-3 (grounded in the ruling, not invented):\n- The ruling requires a stuck gate to page \"within ~15 minutes\": 3 consecutive breaching\n  5-min periods fires at exactly 15 min of sustained markers.\n- The discriminator is PERSISTENCE: a sustained failure emits markers on EVERY review\n  attempt (webhook queue + backfill reconciler retry continuously), so an outage breaches\n  every consecutive period; an isolated self-healing marker breaches at most 1 period —\n  or 2 when it straddles a period boundary — and 3-of-3 pages on neither. The house\n  2-of-2 shape (monitoring_ws7.tf, mirror-guard precedent 969acad79b4b) WOULD page on a\n  boundary-straddling transient, and the evidence base shows 5 transients/48h under load,\n  so the extra period is what makes the isolated-marker AC hold.\n- N-of-N consecutive (not N-of-M) because the observability probe publishes a datapoint\n  every 5 min including zeros (systemd timer OnUnitActiveSec=5min,\n  infra/scripts/observability.sh §4 publishes $vnew which is 0 on no new markers), so a\n  healthy period between two transient spikes correctly resets the streak; with\n  treat_missing_data=notBreaching a probe outage stays non-paging (fails safe, matching S5).\n- Calibration assumes deduplicated counts: companion bug f829-152a-b415-44a4 (merged,\n  change 2117 / 9b060923451) removed the logger-copy double emission, so Sum now counts\n  real errors 1:1.\n\nAlso rewrite the alarm_description heredoc: keep the fail-closed rationale (ADR-0013),\nadd the sustained-detection calibration rationale and this ticket id ea5d-4932-8554-4544.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `infra/terraform/monitoring_s4b.tf` — the only file changed (evaluation_periods,\n  datapoints_to_alarm, comments, alarm_description). No new resources, no variables,\n  no other .tf files, no probe/emitter changes.\n- Out of scope: running `terraform apply` (applies are MANUAL per\n  infra/runbooks/provision-restore.md §plan-before-apply); any change to the metric\n  pipeline; other alarms' shapes.\n\n## Testing\n\nTest tier for monitoring .tf changes in this repo (per terraform-drift.yml and prior\nmonitoring_*.tf changes, e.g. 24ec1e6d8ac): static validation — CI has no\nalarm-behavior simulation tier, so the two behavioral ACs are covered by the shape\narithmetic above (3x300s = 15 min; isolated marker breaches ≤2 < 3 periods) plus:\n- Local: `terraform fmt -check -recursive`, `terraform init -backend=false`,\n  `terraform validate` (Terraform 1.10.5, matching CI).\n- CI (Verified gate): repo lint/typecheck/tests as usual; the terraform-drift workflow\n  runs on GitHub PRs + daily cron, not on Gerrit verify — after merge the DAILY drift\n  sweep will FAIL on the non-empty plan until an operator applies; that is the designed\n  committed-but-unapplied signal (workflow header), recorded on the ticket as the\n  application path.\n\n## Application path (recorded per AC)\n\nLanding via Gerrit does NOT apply to AWS. Applies are manual:\ninfra/runbooks/provision-restore.md §\"plan-before-apply on the shared remote backend\"\n(`terraform plan -out plan.tfplan` → review → `terraform apply plan.tfplan`). The daily\nterraform-drift sweep flags the pending apply until the operator runs it. I will not run\nterraform apply myself.\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- [ ] Alarm no longer fires on an isolated self-healing marker; fires within ~15 min of a sustained marker stream (covered by the 3-of-3 shape arithmetic + static validation — see Testing).\n- [ ] Both behaviors covered by whatever test tier monitoring .tf changes get in this repo (terraform fmt/validate locally; drift plan in CI's daily sweep).\n- [ ] Description text updated with rationale + ticket reference.\n- [ ] Application path (auto vs operator apply) explicitly recorded on the ticket (manual operator apply per provision-restore.md; drift sweep flags until applied)."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787441366996063001,"uuid":"3642c8ef-80c2-4721-87d8-e7b43a63c8bc"}